OL,3,APanama Canal to cut number of ships
OL,4,Apassing through due to El Nino
OL,5,
OL,6,FPanama Canal's operator is to cut the
OL,7,Fnumber of vessels passing through the
OL,8,Fkey waterway due to low rainfall caused
OL,9,Fby El Nino.
OL,11,FThe Panama Canal Authority (ACP) told
OL,12,Fshipping firms on Thursday that 32
OL,13,Fvessels a day will be able to pass
OL,14,Fthrough it from 15 September, compared
OL,15,Fto 36 currently.
OL,17,FEl Nino, a pattern of periodical sea
OL,18,Fsurface warming, affects weather
OL,19,Fsystems globally. This year is expected
OL,20,Fto be particularly strong, with its
OL,21,Feffects made more intense by climate
OL,22,Fchange.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,316,300,200,140,0,100
